Modifications made in ZWork include, among others:
- renaming the product, crates, packages, binaries, environment variables,
  configuration paths and protocol identifiers from "goose" to "zwork";
- replacing brand assets, fonts, prompts and user-facing text;
- turning upstream-operated online services (documentation site, update
  feeds, telemetry, OAuth client metadata) into opt-in configuration that is
  disabled by default;
- replacing the LGPL-3.0-licensed ansi_colours dependency with an
  independent MIT-licensed implementation (vendor/ansi_colours);
- removing upstream community, documentation-site and release infrastructure.

